A||||14||Ferrari_cdn||Air Conditioning?||||5||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||07-13-2001||11:33 PM||||I am getting a '84 Fiero.  It gets very hot where I live and I always want to have air conditioning, and if for some reason the car doesn't include it, I am wondering if it is possible to add one and if it is then approximately how much would that cost?<P>Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||07-14-2001||12:00 AM||||It can be added since all Fieros were built on the same line and all have the same holes but I don't think it would be very fun. There are a lot of little things that go along with the a/c system, not just the big parts that we are all used to... I think if it were me and a/c was a big factor, I would just wait for another car...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-14-2001||01:46 PM||||LOL<BR>Dude! It also gets VERY COLD  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>On a side note, I'm considering getting my AC system fixed... The past few days have been kinda warm. A wet warm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||theogre||07-14-2001||06:03 PM||||There are a whole bunch of changes to the electrical system and you have to pull out the whole dash and things to install the AC ducting. <P>We just went over this in another thread. It could be done but don't plan on it being remotely easy.<P>Worse, since this is an 84, you could run into problems unless you have an 84 for a doner. There are a bunch of 84 only type things in the car as far as wiring goes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||07-14-2001||06:08 PM||||Get a A/C unit off the top of a refridgeration truck<P>pull yuour sunroof, and set it in place.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSoul||07-14-2001||07:17 PM||||  Not a bad plan Grinthock!  In Florida that sun roof feels like a magnifying glass most of the time. D*%& what I would give to have a screen to close like in the newer cars!||||reg||12
Z||000006||theogre||07-14-2001||11:04 PM||||Thinking of sunroof.... I was looking at "cling film" window shade sheets at wall mart... they are 12"x14-16". 2 of those I think will cover most of the roof glass and not look horible. I didn't have the cash to grab them last week. I think I'll stop and get a couple this week.||||reg||1
Z||000007||CoolBlue87GT||07-14-2001||11:25 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroSoul:<BR><B> That sun roof feels like a magnifying glass !</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Pontiac made a shield that attached to the sunroof.  It looks just like the headliner.<P>They were stored in the 'trunk' area in a black vinyl 'pouch' above the spare tire.  You might ask around, someone might have one. There very rare.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ferrari_cdn:<BR><B>getting a '84 Fiero...possible to add A/C ?... approximately how much would that cost?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I once bought a 85 Rabbit diesel, had A/C installed for $750. After that the car was a joy to drive. I put another 225 thousand miles on her.<P>I agree with an earlier post, you might want to wait for another Fiero to come up. It's a lot of work to add. I'd guess 1500 or so.<P>Good luck.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
