Z||000014||StuGood||07-17-2001||09:18 AM||||I seem to recall that tgowens posted a picture of the headliner repair in his gold Fiero...  and there seemed to be a shade panel on the inside of the sunroof.<P>If you can't get a ready-made shade, I'm thinking, "How tough could it be to roll  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> your own?"  Get a piece of fiberboard (or some kind of substrate), apply and cure polyester resin, and glue headliner fabric on, just as you would when you repair a headliner.<P>I agree with the rest of you hotheads, it's no fun driving a solar collector in the summertime.||||reg||3
